Hi. Some-time poster here. I wasn't sure if I should post my babble/
bemusement but perhaps you will find some slime more interesting than
all the SPAM going on here.

I was playing a relatively successful Healer going through the mines.
Had a strong pet; could defend myself well with my thrown daggers and
unicorn horn if I had to and my healing spells were strong (didn't
otherwise have a great spell list).

My lovely cat Purr then steps on a polytrap (before I found it; just
luck of where she stepped with me versus where I stepped) and becomes
Purr the Green Slime. At first I think, "Cool! Those are pretty
powerful. You usually don't see those till Gehennom."

But then I realized the problem: Purr is turning the creatures it's
killing into hostile Green Slimes. I'm in a pretty tight area, and
it's dark with no source of light available, so it's tough to keep
track of where the hostile slimes were, though I did safely dagger one
to death from a distance with the help from a Detect Monsters spell (I
was using that to help, but I couldn't be casting it every second). I
didn't try blindness-ESP because I figured Slimes didn't have minds
(probably should have checked). Ultimately however--and I completely
admit because of my own carelessness--I ended up being slimed. Prayer
did save me once but I got reslimed trying to get away and get my pet
up the stairs (hoping to get her re-polyed on the trap).

Realized after checking some spoilers that I probably should have run
up the stairs and jumped on the poly trap, with no other means of
saving myself (prayer timeout nowhere near safe, unihorn doesn't work,
no fire. Not aware of other options), though of course that also
carried its own risks. I'd even thought of that as a possibility, but
was trying to think of a way to preserve the poly trap so I could try
and get Purr back onto it.

And of course I should have been more careful to begin with to keep
the thing from touching me in the first place. I *think* I had a
luckstone already (accidentally skipped my inventory on death, but my
attributes described luck timeout, so one of the grey stones I found
probably was one) so I probably could have forgone further mine
exploration and abandoned the pet, but she'd been such a key to
helping me survive so far I didn't want to leave her.

This did leave a bones file, so future adventurers will have something
interesting to navigate... at least I ran up the stairs so there will
be only one Slime to worry about, not three or four, and that area is
lit.

Ah well. This isn't a death I feel too bad about... could've tried
more things, but at least it was a learning experience. There are
definitely some pets you don't want to have!

Do y'all have any good pet-poly-gone-wrong stories?

